          {
           "id": "520c0fc5",
           "settings": {
            "editor": "<p class=\"lead\">Here are some common questions about air handler installation and repair. If you don’t see yours, get in touch and we’ll be glad to help.</p>"
           },
           "elements": [],
           "isInner": true,
           "widgetType": "text-editor",
           "elType": "widget"
          },
          {
           "id": "520c231c",
           "settings": {
            "html": "<div class=\"ask\"><img class=\"mascot\" src=\"/wp-content/plugins/newman-core/assets/img/NewmanAirLogo_Bear.svg\" alt=\"\"><div><strong>Still wondering about something?</strong><a href=\"tel:+14237537788\">Call (423) 753-7788</a></div></div>"
           },
           "elements": [],
           "isInner": true,
           "widgetType": "html",
           "elType": "widget"
          }
         ],
         "isInner": true,
         "elType": "container"
        },
        {
         "id": "520c49ca",
         "settings": {
          "html": "<div class=\"faq-list\"><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:0\" open><summary>What does an air handler do in an HVAC system?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>The air handler is responsible for moving conditioned air throughout your home. It includes components like the blower motor, fan, and filters that keep air circulating. Without it, your HVAC system can’t distribute heating or cooling effectively.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:1\"><summary>How do I know if my air handler needs repair?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>Signs include weak airflow, loud noises, musty odors, or uneven room temperatures. A sudden spike in energy bills can also point to a problem. If you notice these issues, a technician should check your system.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:2\"><summary>How long does an air handler last?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>With regular maintenance, most air handlers last 10 to 15 years. Usage, air quality, and maintenance all play a role in lifespan. Replacing older units often improves efficiency and comfort.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:3\"><summary>Can an air handler be repaired, or does it need replacement?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>Many problems can be repaired, such as faulty motors or clogged filters. If the unit is older or has significant damage, replacement may be more cost-effective. Our team will provide honest recommendations based on your system’s condition.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:0\"><summary>Will a new air handler lower my energy bills?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>Yes, newer models are designed for efficiency and can reduce energy use. A properly matched air handler also helps your HVAC system perform better overall. The savings often offset the cost over time.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:1\"><summary>How often should I schedule maintenance for my air handler?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>It’s best to have your air handler serviced at least once a year. Regular maintenance helps prevent breakdowns, improves efficiency, and extends its lifespan. Seasonal tune-ups can keep everything running smoothly.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:2\"><summary>Can I replace just the air handler without replacing the entire HVAC system?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>In some cases, yes, but compatibility is key. If your HVAC system is older, a full replacement may be recommended for efficiency and performance. A technician can determine the best option for your setup.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:3\"><summary>What’s the difference between an air handler and a furnace?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>An air handler moves air through your home and is often paired with heat pumps or AC systems. A furnace generates heat by burning fuel and then distributes it through ducts. They serve different purposes, but both are essential for comfort.</p></div></details><details class=\"qa reveal\" style=\"--d:0\"><summary>How long does installation or repair take?<span class=\"pm\"><svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></span></summary><div class=\"ans\"><p>Most repairs can be done in a few hours, while installation may take most of the day. The timeline depends on your system and what’s required. We’ll give you an accurate estimate before starting work.</p></div></details></div>"
         },
